# The Zenodo concept DOI is added under `identifiers:` once the first GitHub
# release mints it. Version and date-released are finalised at release time.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-26"
title: "sc_pileup: a reusable single-cell pileup stage for per-cell REF/ALT counts at a site VCF"
abstract: >-
  A small, reusable Snakemake workflow that turns single-cell BAMs into per-cell
  REF/ALT count matrices at a configurable set of sites. It factors the
  expensive, deterministic pileup out of the downstream assignment step so that
  genotype demultiplexing (vireo / demuxlet / freemuxlet / souporcell, in
  snp_demux) can be re-run cheaply from saved pileups, and so the same matrices
  feed malignant-cell / clonal analyses (somatic-variant detection, allelic
  imbalance in CNV/LOH regions, cardelino) when pointed at a somatic / CNV-region
  site VCF. It wraps cellSNP-lite, popscle dsc-pileup, and souporcell (minimap2 +
  vartrix) behind one genotype-free interface, and runs standalone or as a git
  submodule within a DVC-tracked dataset.
type: software
